==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{wikipedia|Grenada (disambiguation)}}

===Etymology===
From anglicization/latinization of {{der|en|fr|Grenade}} upon the island's cession to the United Kingdom under the terms of the {{w|1763 Treaty of Paris}} ending the {{w|Seven Years' War}}, from {{der|en|es|Granada}} and {{m|es|los|Los}} {{m|es|Granadillos}} on Spanish maps from at least the 1520s, from {{m|es|Granada}} in Spain, from {{der|en|ar|غَرْنَاطَة|tr=Ḡarnāṭa}}, originally a suburb of the city. {{doublet|en|Granada}}.

